{#- v3 price macros (WS4; art direction P-a to P-e; engineering 3.2.3; blueprint 6.1). Every printed
    price goes through the gate in lib/pricing.js (filter priceParts, lib/eleventy-ws4.js), so
    production shows a number only when the entry is confirmed AND publish AND not legal_hold.
    No placeholder numeral ever ships: a hidden price prints the fallback words.

    Import (with context, so the macros read the build's price_mode global):
      {% from "v3/price.njk" import priceRow, priceValue with context %}

    priceRow(label, entry, opts), inside a <dl class="v3-prices">:
      {{ priceRow("Front doors", pricing.auto_tint.coverage.two_front_doors.car, { fallback: "Price confirmed on the call" }) }}
    priceValue(entry, opts): the value markup alone, for a table cell.

    entry   one pricing.json entry { amount, status, publish, legal_hold, display, range? }
    opts    { mode, fallback, draft_label, note }
            mode         "production" | "preview"; default the price_mode global, else production
            fallback     the words when the gate hides the price, by context (blueprint 6.1):
                         "Price confirmed on the call" (car), "Priced after a free in-home measure"
                         (home and blinds), "Price after we see it" (small cracks). Default: the
                         lib's generic fallback.
            draft_label  the preview-only tag after a draft number (default "Draft price")
            note         optional one plain line under the label (a benefit line, P-a)

    Output of priceRow: <div class="v3-prow" data-price-block> <dt> label </dt> <dd> value </dd> </div>,
    a valid dl group. "From" is set in t-label text-2 before the number (P-b); the dollar sign is the
    same size as the numerals. No strikethrough, no badge, no "save" (P-e).
    Styling: .v3-prow and .v3-prices rules ship in the prices page bundle today
    (assets/v3/css/prices/55-prices.css); a core copy is requested from the CEO (WS4 log). -#}
{% macro priceValue(entry, opts) -%}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
{%- set mode = o.mode or price_mode or "production" -%}
{%- set p = entry | priceParts(mode) -%}
{%- if p.show -%}
<span class="v3-price">{% if p.from %}<span class="v3-price__from t-label fg-2">From</span> {% endif %}<span class="t-price tnum">{{ p.value | safe }}</span>{% if p.draft %} <span class="v3-price__draft t-label">{{ (o.draft_label or "Draft price") | safe }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
{%- else -%}
<span class="v3-price__fallback fg-2">{{ (o.fallback or p.display) | safe }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro priceRow(label, entry, opts) -%}
{%- set o = opts or {} -%}
{%- set mode = o.mode or price_mode or "production" -%}
<div class="v3-prow" data-price-block data-price-mode="{{ mode }}">
  <dt class="v3-prow__label t-body">{{ label | safe }}{% if o.note %}<span class="v3-prow__note t-label fg-2">{{ o.note | safe }}</span>{% endif %}</dt>
  <dd class="v3-prow__value">{{ priceValue(entry, o) }}</dd>
</div>
{%- endmacro %}
